@startuml
title Basic movement R1 — experimental, no gameplay GUI
hide empty members
package ar.edu.uade.sokoban.level {
  class Level <<record>>
  class Board <<immutable record>> {
    +playerPosition() : Position
    +cellAt(position : Position) : Cell
    +rows() : List<List<Cell>>
    +width() : int
    +height() : int
  }
  class Cell <<immutable record>>
  class Position <<record>>
}
package ar.edu.uade.sokoban.movement {
  enum Direction {
    UP
    DOWN
    LEFT
    RIGHT
    --
    -rowDelta : int
    -columnDelta : int
    ~rowDelta() : int
    ~columnDelta() : int
  }
  enum "MoveResult.Kind" as Kind {
    MOVED
    PUSHED
    BLOCKED
  }
  class MoveResult <<record>> {
    -kind : Kind
    -board : Board
    +kind() : Kind
    +board() : Board
  }
  class MovementEngine <<stateless>> {
    +move(state : Board, direction : Direction) : MoveResult
  }
}
Level --> "1" Board : initial loaded value
Board --> "1..*" Cell : immutable rows
Board ..> Position
MovementEngine ..> Board : reads / constructs validated next state
MovementEngine ..> Cell : replaces occupants, preserves terrain
MovementEngine ..> Position : bounded coordinates
MovementEngine ..> Direction
MovementEngine ..> MoveResult : creates outcome
MoveResult --> "1" Board : resulting state
MoveResult --> Kind
note bottom of MovementEngine
Functional experiment: Board + Direction -> MoveResult.
MOVED/PUSHED: new validated Board. BLOCKED: same Board.
No retained current state, counters, history or Undo.
Only normal boxes, floor, goals, walls and bounds.
end note
note bottom of Board
Existing Level Loading aggregate, unchanged.
Prior Boards / loaded Level remain immutable.
No additional GameState wrapper in this subset.
end note
note bottom of MoveResult
Data only; engine establishes transition semantics.
Records validate non-null values.
Design remains experimental, without team ratification.
end note
package "Runtime individual R2" {
  class RuntimeState <<immutable record>> {
    +terrain() : List<List<Ground>>
    +player() : Position
    +boxes() : List<Box>
    +locks() : List<Lock>
    +walls() : List<DynamicWall>
    +lockActive(id : String) : boolean
    +wallOpen(position : Position) : boolean
    +fromLevel(level : Level) : RuntimeState
    +fromDefinition(definition : ExperimentalFragileLevel) : RuntimeState
    +boxAt(position : Position) : Box
  }
  class "RuntimeState.Box" as RuntimeBox <<record>>
  class "RuntimeState.Lock" as RuntimeLock <<record>>
  class "RuntimeState.DynamicWall" as RuntimeWall <<record>>
  class "RuntimeMoveResult.LockChange" as LockChange <<record>>
  enum "RuntimeState.Ground" as Ground
  enum "RuntimeState.BoxKind" as BoxKind
  class RuntimeMovementEngine <<stateless>> {
    +move(state : RuntimeState, direction : Direction) : RuntimeMoveResult
  }
  class RuntimeMoveResult <<record>> {
    +state() : RuntimeState
    +pushedBox() : Box
    +boxDestination() : Position
    +boxDistance() : int
    +broken() : boolean
    +lockChanges() : List<LockChange>
  }
}
RuntimeState --> "0..*" RuntimeLock
RuntimeState --> "0..*" RuntimeWall
RuntimeWall ..> RuntimeLock : associated IDs
RuntimeMoveResult --> "0..*" LockChange
RuntimeState --> "0..*" RuntimeBox
RuntimeState --> Ground
RuntimeBox --> BoxKind
RuntimeMovementEngine ..> RuntimeState
RuntimeMovementEngine ..> Direction
RuntimeMovementEngine ..> RuntimeMoveResult
RuntimeMoveResult --> RuntimeState
RuntimeMoveResult --> RuntimeBox
note bottom of RuntimeState
Independent immutable runtime, not Board projection.
ICE, Lock and dynamic walls are programmatic.
Walls derive openness from associated locks.
TXT and Swing remain unchanged; Observer is pending.
end note
@enduml
